==Threshold of originality== <!--T:49-->

</translate><noinclude>{{CRT shortcut|TOO|Indonesia|anchor=no}}</noinclude>
<translate>

<!--T:50-->
Probably {{NotMark}} for most logos.

<!--T:62-->
Indonesian law frames protectable works as creations that are "unique and personal" and that "result from inspiration, ability, thought, imagination, dexterity, skill or expertise" expressed in a tangible form.{{sref|Undang-Undang No. 28/2014}}

<!--T:56-->
The statute expressly enumerates categories of protected works, including photographic works, portraits and architectural works (including building design and technical drawings), and applied art; by contrast the law excludes unfixed ideas, procedures, systems, methods and objects whose form serves only a functional purpose.

<!--T:57-->
In practice Indonesia's threshold of originality has frequently been described as comparatively low; administrative recordation practice and scholarly commentary note that registrations and recordations have included items such as wallpaper, wrappers, packaging designs and technical drawings, producing an overlap between copyright and design practice that editors should treat cautiously when deciding whether an image is a copyrightable artistic work or a utilitarian/functional object.<ref>{{cite book |last=Antons |first=Christoph |title=Copyright law reform and the information society in Indonesia |editor=Brian Fitzgerald; Fuping Gao; Damien O'Brien; Sampsung Xiaoxiang Shi |publisher=Sydney University Press |year=2008 |pages=235–255 |url=https://open.sydneyuniversitypress.com.au/files/9781920898724.pdf |accessdate=2025-08-12}}</ref>

<!--T:63-->
The ASEAN flag was successfully deleted in [[Commons:Deletion requests/File:Flag of ASEAN.svg]] on the grounds that ASEAN is headquartered in Jakarta and that ASEAN claims copyright over their flag, so it is reasonable to assume that the Indonesian government recognizes the copyright for that flag.

==Algorithmic and AI-created works== <!--T:58-->

<!--T:59-->
2014 Copyright Law does not have a specific section for algorithmic and AI-created works but in general, a work must be created by human in order to be able to register the copyright. An informal discussion with a law firm has came to this conclusion.<ref name=IndAI/>

